From 5833be15b757354ecde6b8488dcbe4dc7f30ec61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:41:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Viewer track: world matrices for the pose check (wf, wi, ws),
 behind MSL_VIEWER_TRACK_WORLD

With MSL_VIEWER_TRACK_WORLD=1 in the environment as the track is made, each
fighter part's, item joint's and stage joint's world matrix at the frame's
end is written, made as HSD_JObjMakeMatrix makes it (its scale
compensation, HSD_MtxSRT, HSD_MtxSRTQuat, HSD_MtxSRTConcat) in the track's
own storage, so nothing of the match changes. Joints the game places
another way (RObjs, IK, user and independent matrices, path animations),
cold fighter parts and the parts of stopped stage animations are left out
with everything under them. Off, nothing is written or allocated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017JX71xgnBPBiwucag1mFRr
---
